# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT REAL DATA.
#
# kpi-raw/    holds fetched PR bodies, review comments and author identities.
# kpi-reports/ holds per-person metrics and quality scores.
#
# Both are performance-review-adjacent data about identifiable colleagues, and
# both are ignored wholesale. Synthetic, publishable examples live in samples/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
kpi-raw/
kpi-reports/

# The real team roster holds colleague email addresses. teams.example.json is the
# committed placeholder; teams.json is yours and stays local.
teams.json

# Anything else that looks like collected data
*-summary.json
*-prs.csv
*-members.csv
*-team.html
kpi-ledger.csv
team-ledger.csv
*-talking-points.md
*.local.json

# ...but the synthetic examples in samples/ are meant to be published
!samples/example-prs.csv
!samples/example-ledger.csv
!samples/example-team-members.csv
!samples/example-team-report.html

